OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGLITHUANIA MAY FACE DIRECT
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGRULE FROM MOSCOW
OL,4,D
OL,5, President Gorbachev has said he would
OL,6, consider using his new power of direct
OL,7, presidential rule over Lithuania.
OL,9,FMr Gorbachev was given the power when
OL,10,Fselected for the new-style executive
OL,11,Fpresidency, but he said he would only
OL,12,Fuse it as "an extreme measure".
OL,13,F
OL,14,FMr Gorbachev said a referendum should
OL,15,Fbe held in Lithuania. He thought most
OL,16,FLithuanians favoured more independence
OL,17,Fwithin the framework of the USSR.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FMeanwhile, a leader of the pro-Moscow
OL,20,FLithuanian communist party has said the
OL,21,FKremlin is not being tough enough.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG10-04-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
