OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGHURD URGES MOSCOW TO
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGTALK TO LITHUANIA
OL,4,F
OL,5, Foreign Secretary Douglas Hurd has
OL,6, urged the Kremlin to open talks with
OL,7, the Baltic republic of Lithuania.
OL,9,FIn an after dinner speech he said
OL,10,FLithuanians had expressed clearly their
OL,11,Fwish for independence and advised
OL,12,F"purposeful negotiations".
OL,14,FEarlier, Mr Hurd met Soviet President
OL,15,FMikhail Gorbachev but would not reveal
OL,16,Fany details of their conversation which
OL,17,Fhe said was based on confidentiality.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FMr Hurd is in Moscow for extensive
OL,20,Ftalks with Soviet foreign minister
OL,21,FEduard Shevardnadze.
OL,23,D]FFromG10-04-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
