OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGIMPROVED BR PAY
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGOFFER "UNACCEPTABLE"
OL,5, Rail union leaders have indicated they
OL,6, will reject British Rail's latest 8.5%
OL,7, pay offer after talks between unions
OL,8, and British Rail were adjourned.
OL,10,FJimmy Knapp, General Secretary of the
OL,11,FNational Union of Railwaymen, said
OL,12,Fafter the talks that the deal was
OL,13,F"not acceptable".
OL,14,F
OL,15,FFurther talks will be held after Easter
OL,16,Fbetween BR and the three rail unions
OL,17,Finvolved.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FThe unions want a "substantial" pay
OL,20,Fincrease and a four-hour cut in the
OL,21,Fworking week, bringing it to 35 hours.
OL,23,D]FFromG10-04-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,190,120,250,0,100
PN,18109
SC,0009
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1775831159
OL,1,Vk4                               G9/9
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGEMS MEMBERSHIP "PAINFUL",
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGSAYS WALTERS
OL,5, Sir Alan Walters, former economic
OL,6, adviser to Mrs Thatcher, has attacked
OL,7, the European Monetary System.
OL,9,FSir Alan, whose opposition to the EMS
OL,10,Fled to Nigel Lawson's resignation as
OL,11,FChancellor, said EMS membership was
OL,12,F"painful for democracy".
OL,13,F
OL,14,FHe said while it might work for a while
OL,15,Fit would "ultimately sow the seeds of
OL,16,Fits own destruction".
OL,17,F
OL,18,FSir Alan was speaking at London's City
OL,19,FUniversity in his first major speech
OL,20,Fsince his resignation last October.
OL,22,D]F This Ceefax page is fromG10-04-90
